and 2.", :decision :reuse}, :selected-reference #propagators.ids.NodeId {:uuid #uuid "39b6be29-d9bb-3443-8f4c-fefcf4d53e04"}, :selected-callable true, :selection-validation :available-callable, :request-count 7, :identity {:id #uuid "7f0f0884-10e4-45d2-99f0-3856bbbae823", :run-id #uuid "a8915180-3a11-4639-ab45-fd2e394541dc"}, :child #propagators.ids.NodeId {:uuid #uuid "4aec2486-39d2-3858-90ce-879c4a676e91"}} {:round 4, :record {:relations "Progressive tier pricing: first 100 at $2, next 400 at $1.60, remainder at $1.30. Rush adds 20% of production. Member discount is 10% of (production+rush), capped at discount-cap. Setup fee added after discount. Delivery waived if subtotal>=250. Tax 8% on (subtotal+delivery). Final total rounded half-up to cents.", :tests "Verify production=180 (90*2), rush=36 (0.2*180), discount=21.6 (0.1*216, under cap 40), subtotal=219.4, delivery=12 (219.4<250), tax=18.512, total=249.91.", :steps "1. Invoke compute-quote with quantity-4, rush-4, member-4, discount-cap-4. 2. Connect each output slot to quote-4. 3. Build text reply connecting to user-output-4.", :operators "compute-quote (existing network), struct, slot, ->, str, round-money, min, max, select, +, -, *, /, >=, =", :status "ready", :outputs "A quote struct (quote-4) with slots :production, :rush, :discount, :subtotal, :delivery, :tax, :total, and a text reply (user-output-4) showing the charge breakdown and final total.", :operator "compute-quote", :units "All monetary values in dollars. Quantities in copies. Rates are dimensionless multipliers. Tax-rate and rush-rate and member-rate are unitless fractions.", :unknowns "None. All inputs for this order are known. The compute-quote callable is available and proven correct on three prior orders.", :facts "quantity-4=90, rush-4=true, member-4=true, discount-cap-4=40. Shared pricing: tier-one-limit=100, tier-two-count=400, tier-one-price=2, tier-two-price=1.60M, tier-three-price=1.30M, rush-rate=0.20M, member-rate=0.10M, setup-fee=25, delivery-fee=12, free-delivery-threshold=250, tax-rate=0.08M. compute-quote network already defined and successfully applied in rounds 1-3.", :decision :reuse}, :selected-reference #propagators.ids.NodeId {:uuid #uuid "39b6be29-d9bb-3443-8f4c-fefcf4d53e04"}, :selected-callable true, :selection-validation :available-callable, :request-count 10, :identity {:id #uuid "7f0f0884-10e4-45d2-99f0-3856bbbae823", :run-id #uuid "a8915180-3a11-4639-ab45-fd2e394541dc"}, :child #propagators.ids.NodeId {:uuid #uuid "4aec2486-39d2-3858-90ce-879c4a676e91"}} {:round 5, :record {:relations "progressive tier pricing; rush = rush-rate * production; discount = min(member-rate*(production+rush), discount-cap); subtotal = production+rush+setup-discount; delivery waived if subtotal>=threshold; tax = tax-rate*(subtotal+delivery); total = round-money(subtotal+delivery+tax)", :tests "Verify discount is capped at 75 (raw would be 135.12); verify delivery is 0 since subtotal exceeds 250; verify total rounds correctly", :steps "Invoke compute-quote with quantity-5, rush-5, member-5, discount-cap-5. Connect resulting struct slots to quote-5. Build text reply for user-output-5.", :operators "compute-quote (existing callable), min, max, select, +, -, *, round-money, str, struct, slot, ->", :status "ready", :outputs "production, rush charge, discount, subtotal, delivery, tax, total (rounded to cents) for 720 copies, member, rush, discount-cap $75", :operator "compute-quote", :units "dollars for prices/fees/charges, copies for quantity, dimensionless multipliers for rates", :unknowns "Computed production, rush, discount, subtotal, delivery, tax, total for this specific order", :facts "quantity-5=720, rush-5=true, member-5=true, discount-cap-5=75 (promotion), tier-one-limit=100, tier-one-price=2, tier-two-count=400, tier-two-price=1.60, tier-three-price=1.30, rush-rate=0.20, member-rate=0.10, setup-fee=25, delivery-fee=12, free-delivery-threshold=250, tax-rate=0.08. compute-quote already defined as (network [quantity rush? member? discount-cap] ...)", :decision :reuse}, :selected-reference #propagators.ids.NodeId {:uuid #uuid "39b6be29-d9bb-3443-8f4c-fefcf4d53e04"}, :selected-callable true, :selection-validation :available-callable, :request-count 13, :identity {:id #uuid "7f0f0884-10e4-45d2-99f0-3856bbbae823", :run-id #uuid "a8915180-3a11-4639-ab45-fd2e394541dc"}, :child #propagators.ids.NodeId {:uuid #uuid "4aec2486-39d2-3858-90ce-879c4a676e91"}}], :generalization-records [{:round 1, :record {:interface "Compose the computation from existing primitives (+, -, *, select, min, max, round-money, >=, <) reading shared constants from the pricing struct's slots and per-order values from order-1's slots. No new callable is required for correctness, but a small network taking (quantity, rush?, member?, discount-cap) and closing over pricing slots would enable reuse across questions 2-5 without re-deriving the formula. The pricing struct already exists as the shared-rule carrier; the computation is a direct composition of arithmetic and select over its slots. This is the simplest suitable interface: no abstraction beyond the existing pricing struct is warranted.", :problem-class "Tiered unit-price quotation with conditional surcharges (rush), conditional discounts (membership with cap), fixed fees (setup, delivery with threshold waiver), and ad-valorem tax. Applies to any print-shop order with varying quantity, service level, and membership status.", :relations "production = tiered(quantity); rush-charge = rush-rate * production if rush?; discount = member-rate * (production + rush-charge) if member? capped at discount-cap, else 0; subtotal = production + rush-charge - discount + setup-fee; delivery = delivery-fee if subtotal < free-delivery-threshold else 0; tax = tax-rate * (subtotal + delivery); total = round-money(subtotal + delivery + tax).", :tests "Verify production=160, rush=0, discount=0, subtotal=185, delivery=12, tax=15.76, total=212.76. Check that a quantity of 150 would split across tiers. Check member discount capping. Check free-delivery waiver at threshold.", :captured "Shared numeric rules captured in the pricing struct: tier-one-limit, tier-one-price, tier-two-count, tier-two-price, tier-three-price, rush-rate, member-rate, setup-fee, delivery-fee, free-delivery-threshold, tax-rate. These are constant across all orders and identified by the shared-rule premise.", :steps "1. Read shared rules from pricing struct slots. 2. Compute tiered production cost for 80 copies (all in tier-one). 3. Rush charge = 0 (standard). 4. Discount = 0 (nonmember). 5. Subtotal = production + rush - discount + setup-fee. 6. Delivery = 12 since subtotal < 250. 7. Tax = 0.08 * (subtotal + delivery). 8. Total = round-money(subtotal + delivery + tax). 9. Connect to quote-1 slots and user-output-1.", :operators "+ - * / min max select = >= <= str round-money struct slot -> network define ttms-premise-closure", :status "ready", :outputs "A quote struct (quote-1) with slots :production, :rush, :discount, :subtotal, :delivery, :tax, :total and a text reply (user-output-1) showing the charges and final total.", :operator "pricing", :units "Dollars for all monetary values; copies for quantity; rates are dimensionless multipliers.", :unknowns "None for this question; all inputs are known. Future orders (2-5) are unknown.", :facts "quantity-1=80, member-1=false, rush-1=false, discount-cap-1=40, tier-one-limit=100, tier-one-price=2, tier-two-count=400, tier-two-price=1.60M, tier-three-price=1.30M, rush-rate=0.20M, member-rate=0.10M, setup-fee=25, delivery-fee=12, free-delivery-threshold=250, tax-rate=0.08M. All 80 copies fall within tier-one-limit (100), so production = 80*2 = 160. Nonmember means no discount. Standard service means no rush charge. Subtotal after discount+setup = 160+25 = 185 < 250, so delivery fee applies. Tax applies to (subtotal+delivery). Final total rounded to cents.", :parameters "Per-order variables: quantity (integer copies), rush? (boolean), member? (boolean), discount-cap (dollar cap on member discount). These vary across questions 1-5.", :decision :compose}, :selected-reference #propagators.ids.NodeId {:uuid #uuid "3ed45fc7-f535-36c9-8f4e-48b52063da1d"}, :selected-callable false, :selection-validation :unavailable-or-not-callable, :request-count 2, :identity {:id #uuid "7f0f0884-10e4-45d2-99f0-3856bbbae823", :run-id #uuid "a8915180-3a11-4639-ab45-fd2e394541dc"}, :child #propagators.ids.NodeId {:uuid #uuid "4aec2486-39d2-3858-90ce-879c4a676e91"}} {:round 2, :record {:interface "Direct reuse of the existing compute-quote callable. It was defined in round 1 as a network taking [quantity rush? member? discount-cap] and returning a struct with all seven quote slots. The shared pricing rules are already bound as cells in the lexical environment, so the callable resolves them at invocation time. No adaptation or new construction is needed; the current order's four parameters are simply passed as arguments. This is the simplest suitable interface because the callable is already fully general over the varying inputs and correctly captures the fixed rules.", :problem-class "Any print-shop quote request parameterized by quantity, rush flag, member flag, and a per-order discount cap, under a fixed set of tiered pricing and fee rules.", :relations "Progressive tier pricing on quantity; rush adds rush-rate*production; member discount is member-rate*(production+rush) capped at discount-cap; setup-fee added after discount; delivery waived if subtotal>=free-delivery-threshold; tax applied to subtotal+delivery; final total rounded half-up to cents.", :tests "Verify production=424, rush=84.80, discount=40 (capped), subtotal=493.80, delivery=0 (>=250), tax=39.504, total=533.30. Check discount is capped at 40 not 50.88.", :captured "The shared pricing rules (tier-one-limit, tier-one-price, tier-two-count, tier-two-price, tier-three-price, rush-rate, member-rate, setup-fee, delivery-fee, free-delivery-threshold, tax-rate) are captured as cell references inside the compute-quote network body. The progressive-tier logic, rush surcharge formula, member-discount-with-cap formula, setup-fee addition, delivery-waiver threshold, tax application, and final rounding are all fixed algorithmic structure.", :steps "1. Invoke compute-quote with quantity-2, rush-2, member-2, discount-cap-2. 2. Connect each slot of the result struct to quote-2 slots. 3. Build a text summary and connect to user-output-2.", :operators "compute-quote, struct, slot, ->, str, min, max, select, round-money, +, -, *, /, >=, =", :status "ready", :outputs "A quote struct with :production, :rush, :discount, :subtotal, :delivery, :tax, :total for 240 copies, member, rush; plus a text summary on user-output-2.", :operator "compute-quote", :units "Dollars for monetary values; copies for quantity; rates are dimensionless multipliers.", :unknowns "None; all inputs for this order are known.", :facts "quantity-2=240, rush-2=true, member-2=true, discount-cap-2=40. Shared rules: tier-one-limit=100, tier-one-price=2, tier-two-count=400, tier-two-price=1.60M, tier-three-price=1.30M, rush-rate=0.20M, member-rate=0.10M, setup-fee=25, delivery-fee=12, free-delivery-threshold=250, tax-rate=0.08M. compute-quote network already defined and tested on round 1.", :parameters "quantity (copies), rush? (boolean), member? (boolean), discount-cap (dollars) — these are the per-order varying inputs supplied as cells.", :decision :reuse}, :selected-reference #propagators.ids.NodeId {:uuid #uuid "39b6be29-d9bb-3443-8f4c-fefcf4d53e04"}, :selected-callable true, :selection-validation :available-callable, :request-count 5, :identity {:id #uuid "7f0f0884-10e4-45d2-99f0-3856bbbae823", :run-id #uuid "a8915180-3a11-4639-ab45-fd2e394541dc"}, :child #propagators.ids.NodeId {:uuid #uuid "4aec2486-39d2-3858-90ce-879c4a676e91"}} {:round 3, :record {:interface "Direct reuse of the existing compute-quote callable. It was constructed in round 1 as a general network parameterized on the four order-specific inputs, with all shared rules baked into its body. Rounds 1 and 2 confirmed correct behavior on nonmember-standard and member-rush cases. No adaptation or new construction is warranted; the interface already separates variable inputs from captured assumptions cleanly. Generalization beyond this callable would add unnecessary complexity since every future order differs only in these four parameters.", :problem-class "Any single print-shop order quote: given a quantity, rush flag, membership flag, and a per-order discount cap, compute the full charge breakdown (production, rush, discount, subtotal, delivery, tax, total) under the shared progressive-tier pricing rules.", :relations "Progressive tier pricing on production; rush adds rush-rate*production; member discount is member-rate*(production+rush) capped at discount-cap; setup-fee added after discount; delivery waived if subtotal>=free-delivery-threshold; tax applied to subtotal+delivery; final total rounded half-up to cents.", :tests "Verify production=1126, rush=0, discount=40 (capped), subtotal=1111, delivery=0, tax=88.88, total=1199.88.", :captured "The shared pricing rules are captured inside the compute-quote network body: tier-one-limit=100, tier-one-price=2, tier-two-count=400, tier-two-price=1.60, tier-three-price=1.30, rush-rate=0.20, member-rate=0.10, setup-fee=25, delivery-fee=12, free-delivery-threshold=250, tax-rate=0.08. These are constant across all orders and need not be re-specified per invocation.", :steps "1. Invoke compute-quote with quantity-3, rush-3, member-3, discount-cap-3. 2. Connect each slot of the result struct to the corresponding slot of quote-3. 3. Build a text summary and connect to user-output-3.", :operators "compute-quote, struct, slot, ->, str, min, max, +, -, *, select, >=, round-money", :status "ready", :outputs "A quote struct with :production, :rush, :discount, :subtotal, :delivery, :tax, :total for 720 copies, member, standard service, plus a text summary on user-output-3.", :operator "compute-quote", :units "Dollars for monetary values; copies for quantity; rates are dimensionless multipliers.", :unknowns "None; all inputs for this order are known.", :facts "quantity-3=720, member-3=true, rush-3=false, discount-cap-3=40. Shared rules: tier-one-limit=100, tier-one-price=2, tier-two-count=400, tier-two-price=1.60M, tier-three-price=1.30M, rush-rate=0.20M, member-rate=0.10M, setup-fee=25, delivery-fee=12, free-delivery-threshold=250, tax-rate=0.08M. compute-quote network already defined and used in rounds 1 and 2.", :parameters "quantity (copies), rush? (boolean), member? (boolean), discount-cap (dollars). These are the only quantities that vary between orders; they are already the four parameters of compute-quote.", :decision :reuse}, :selected-reference #propagators.ids.NodeId {:uuid #uuid "39b6be29-d9bb-3443-8f4c-fefcf4d53e04"}, :selected-callable true, :selection-validation :available-callable, :request-count 8, :identity {:id #uuid "7f0f0884-10e4-45d2-99f0-3856bbbae823", :run-id #uuid "a8915180-3a11-4639-ab45-fd2e394541dc"}, :child #propagators.ids.NodeId {:uuid #uuid "4aec2486-39d2-3858-90ce-879c4a676e91"}} {:round 4, :record {:interface "Direct reuse of the existing compute-quote network. It already parameterizes exactly the four order-varying inputs and captures all shared pricing assumptions. It has been invoked successfully on three prior orders (80/nonmember/standard, 240/member/rush, 720/member/standard) producing correct results. No adaptation or new construction is warranted; the simplest suitable interface is the one already in the binding directory.", :problem-class "Print-shop quote computation: given a quantity, rush flag, membership flag, and discount cap, produce a full charge breakdown (production, rush, discount, subtotal, delivery, tax, total) under a fixed progressive-tier pricing schedule with surcharges, discounts, fees, and tax.", :relations "Progressive tier pricing: first 100 at $2, next 400 at $1.60, remainder at $1.30. Rush adds 20% of production. Member discount is 10% of (production+rush), capped at discount-cap. Setup fee added after discount. Delivery waived if subtotal>=250. Tax 8% on (subtotal+delivery). Final total rounded half-up to cents.", :tests "Verify production=180 (90*2), rush=36 (0.2*180), discount=21.6 (0.1*216, under cap 40), subtotal=219.4, delivery=12 (219.4<250), tax=18.512, total=249.91.", :captured "The shared pricing schedule (tier-one-limit=100, tier-two-count=400, tier-one-price=2, tier-two-price=1.60, tier-three-price=1.30), surcharge rates (rush-rate=0.20, member-rate=0.10), fixed fees (setup-fee=25, delivery-fee=12), free-delivery-threshold=250, and tax-rate=0.08 are captured inside the network body. These are shared-rule premises valid across all orders and do not change between questions.", :steps "1. Invoke compute-quote with quantity-4, rush-4, member-4, discount-cap-4. 2. Connect each output slot to quote-4. 3. Build text reply connecting to user-output-4.", :operators "compute-quote (existing network), struct, slot, ->, str, round-money, min, max, select, +, -, *, /, >=, =", :status "ready", :outputs "A quote struct (quote-4) with slots :production, :rush, :discount, :subtotal, :delivery, :tax, :total, and a text reply (user-output-4) showing the charge breakdown and final total.", :operator "compute-quote", :units "All monetary values in dollars. Quantities in copies. Rates are dimensionless multipliers. Tax-rate and rush-rate and member-rate are unitless fractions.", :unknowns "None. All inputs for this order are known. The compute-quote callable is available and proven correct on three prior orders.", :facts "quantity-4=90, rush-4=true, member-4=true, discount-cap-4=40. Shared pricing: tier-one-limit=100, tier-two-count=400, tier-one-price=2, tier-two-price=1.60M, tier-three-price=1.30M, rush-rate=0.20M, member-rate=0.10M, setup-fee=25, delivery-fee=12, free-delivery-threshold=250, tax-rate=0.08M. compute-quote network already defined and successfully applied in rounds 1-3.", :parameters "quantity (integer copies), rush? (boolean), member? (boolean), discount-cap (dollar amount). These four values vary per order and are the only inputs the caller must supply.", :decision :reuse}, :selected-reference #propagators.ids.NodeId {:uuid #uuid "39b6be29-d9bb-3443-8f4c-fefcf4d53e04"}, :selected-callable true, :selection-validation :available-callable, :request-count 11, :identity {:id #uuid "7f0f0884-10e4-45d2-99f0-3856bbbae823", :run-id #uuid "a8915180-3a11-4639-ab45-fd2e394541dc"}, :child #propagators.ids.NodeId {:uuid #uuid "4aec2486-39d2-3858-90ce-879c4a676e91"}} {:round 5, :record {:interface "Direct reuse of the existing compute-quote callable. It already exposes quantity, rush?, member?, and discount-cap as parameters, so the $75 promotional cap is simply a different argument value—no adaptation or construction is needed. The network encapsulates all rule logic and returns a struct with the seven output slots. This is the simplest suitable interface; generalizing further (e.g., parameterizing tier boundaries or rates) would add complexity without addressing any observed variation in the problem set.", :problem-class "Print-shop quote computation: given a quantity, service options (rush, membership), and a discount cap, compute a full charge breakdown using progressive tier pricing, surcharges, discounts, fees, and tax. The class covers any combination of these four inputs under a fixed rule set.", :relations "progressive tier pricing; rush = rush-rate * production; discount = min(member-rate*(production+rush), discount-cap); subtotal = production+rush+setup-discount; delivery waived if subtotal>=threshold; tax = tax-rate*(subtotal+delivery); total = round-money(subtotal+delivery+tax)", :tests "Verify discount is capped at 75 (raw would be 135.12); verify delivery is 0 since subtotal exceeds 250; verify total rounds correctly", :captured "The pricing rule constants (tier-one-limit=100, tier-one-price=2, tier-two-count=400, tier-two-price=1.60, tier-three-price=1.30, rush-rate=0.20, member-rate=0.10, setup-fee=25, delivery-fee=12, free-delivery-threshold=250, tax-rate=0.08) and the structural relationships (progressive tiers, rush surcharge formula, discount formula with cap, delivery waiver logic, tax application, final rounding) are fixed assumptions embedded in the compute-quote network body. They remain valid across all orders unless the shop changes its rules.", :steps "Invoke compute-quote with quantity-5, rush-5, member-5, discount-cap-5. Connect resulting struct slots to quote-5. Build text reply for user-output-5.", :operators "compute-quote (existing callable), min, max, select, +, -, *, round-money, str, struct, slot, ->", :status "ready", :outputs "production, rush charge, discount, subtotal, delivery, tax, total (rounded to cents) for 720 copies, member, rush, discount-cap $75", :operator "compute-quote", :units "dollars for prices/fees/charges, copies for quantity, dimensionless multipliers for rates", :unknowns "Computed production, rush, discount, subtotal, delivery, tax, total for this specific order", :facts "quantity-5=720, rush-5=true, member-5=true, discount-cap-5=75 (promotion), tier-one-limit=100, tier-one-price=2, tier-two-count=400, tier-two-price=1.60, tier-three-price=1.30, rush-rate=0.20, member-rate=0.10, setup-fee=25, delivery-fee=12, free-delivery-threshold=250, tax-rate=0.08. compute-quote already defined as (network [quantity rush? member? discount-cap] ...)", :parameters "quantity (copies), rush? (boolean), member? (boolean), discount-cap (dollars). These four values vary per order and are the only inputs that change between questions.", :decision :reuse}, :selected-reference #propagators.ids.NodeId {:uuid #uuid "39b6be29-d9bb-3443-8f4c-fefcf4d53e04"}, :selected-callable true, :selection-validation :available-callable, :request-count 14, :identity {:id #uuid "7f